  "interpretation": "Further mechanism development on the consumed, retrospectively selected 2019 cohort. A 20-session stock/index return window ending at each declared t-minus-two cutoff estimates OLS beta and index sample volatility. A same-seed/date common uniform standardized innovation has mean zero and theoretical variance one; it is synthetic, not actual target-day return/news. Public valuation is beta times lagged index volatility times the common innovation, in bps, risk multiplier one and cap 500 bps, belief scale 1000. Negative/zero beta is retained; missing source or zero index variance fails explicitly. The unchanged private stock-risk innovation remains present: public addition increases total valuation variance and is not a fixed-marginal-variance covariance recovery. Target channel changes only strategy beliefs/allocation; physical quote channel changes strategies and all backgrounds. Background quantity targets, private receipts, finite resources, core allocation and auction remain frozen. Same-state records contain decisions and submitted orders only, no hypothetical acceptance/fills/prices. All four public cells cross both inventory anchors, original/all-off own-price feedback and all five seeds; no selection or gain fitting. Existing tolerances are descriptive development checks, not investor calibration, unused-period validation or permission to claim policy forecasts. Earlier native renderer hash/source-PDF QC exceptions remain; no new PDF parsing/rendering is used. Small implementation fixtures and full-panel input bounds were inspected before freeze.",
